msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/ch3-the-reference-architecture-for-d/p-3-5-3-2-c33109.md:2
msgid "Public Health Surveillance Platform — supports the detection, monitoring, and reporting of conditions and events across populations."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/ch3-the-reference-architecture-for-d/p-3-1-785029.md:1
msgid "Rather than define a new vocabulary, the reference architecture is expressed using <a0>ArchiMate®</a0>, an open modelling language for <a1>enterprise architecture</a1> maintained by The Open Group.2 ArchiMate® provides defined types of element — among them goals, capabilities, services, application components, and <a2>data objects</a2> — and defined types of relationship between them, organised across business, application, and technology layers — broadly aligning with the architecture domains of established enterprise-architecture practice1 — together with motivation elements that capture why an element matters and to whom. Drawing on an established language brings several practical benefits. Each element has a defined type with clear meaning, so that a capability, a component, and a service are not confused with one another. The architecture can be authored, checked, and published using widely available tools. Because the language is broadly adopted, descriptions expressed in it can be read and compared across organisations and countries without translation. And the typed relationships make it possible to trace from goals, through the capabilities that serve them, to the components that realise them — a property that matters for governance and for assessing whether the architecture is delivering on its goals."
msgstr ""

#: folio/dpi-h-ra/ch3-the-reference-architecture-for-d/p-3-5-3-f22754.md:21
msgid "Real-time clinical and entitlement support (Foundational Layer → Business Services → Point of Service): Business-service components consume that resolved, coded context: the Computable Decision Support Engine (CDSE) evaluates the patient's coded record against computable clinical guidelines to return point-of-care recommendations; the Benefits Package Registry (BPR) provides the covered services and entitlement rules that financing and clinical systems apply; and the Supplier Registry links authorised suppliers to the products recorded in the Product Registry."
msgstr ""

